[ti:Clothes Off The Lie]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:1984s.text - Rectified]
[length:04:13.99]

[01:04.21]West light on the rabbit ground
[01:07.71]Elm-shadow moving like her hair let down
[01:11.52]A quiet stream, the afternoon holds still
[01:14.33]And she walks toward me, throwing the years off
[01:18.99]No screen out here, no one to own this hour
[01:22.78]The rented room can wait; this field is ours
[01:25.97]She doesn't look back. She doesn't explain
[01:29.45]One movement and the city falls away
[01:34.50]She tore the clothes off the lie... in one perfect move
[01:41.93]She tore the clothes off the lie... and the whole world came loose
[01:49.14]The Party, the watchers, the years we never lived through
[01:55.36]That act was political... and it was true
[02:03.50]Instrumental
[02:06.79]A glass paperweight, a room above the yard
[02:10.88]We called it ours. We should have kept our guard
[02:13.60]A kind voice at the door, a glass of dark wine
[02:17.79]He said we had friends. He said we would be fine
[02:22.47]Come in, Winston. You've been expected
[02:27.14]There are friends here. You have nothing to fear
[02:33.69]She tore the clothes off the lie... in one perfect move
[02:41.00]She tore the clothes off the lie... and the whole world came loose
[02:48.23]We took the wine and the book and the secret name
[02:53.50]We thought it was freedom. It was only a game
[03:01.86]A van in the street. A step on the stair
[03:05.49]The room was never ours. The friends were never there
[03:08.67]Don't look at the door... it's already too late
[03:12.49]The field was a picture. The wine was a bait
[03:18.79]Instrumental
[03:21.14]She tore the clothes off the lie... we believed it was proof
[03:28.20]Golden for a minute... then the light goes through
[03:31.81]That act was political... they were coming for you
[03:37.59](Ah... ah... ah)
[04:05.61]
